T034 (W1.2, the simulation in a real Web Worker, with the App wiring behind ?simworker=1): cloud/t034, cloud carry-over Nov 3, review fix round Nov 3; report docs/dev/reports/local-W1.2-worker.md; tsc clean, full vitest 2,174 passed, bot 192,899 (dev's reference since B3); tools/qa-worker.mjs on the production build at size 256 with 10-minute soaks: 39 of 39 with ?simwasm=wasm, 35 of 37 without (the 2 FAILs the harness's own, fixed and passed in the wasm run).
Open, for the lead: (1) *(closed by T034b, which corrects this item)* §6's "worker's protector intact after 10 min" is gated in Chromium 153: its V8 has the ArrayBufferDetaching protector and tracks views (a detach of a buffer with no view or one TypedArray view is free; one with two or more views, a DataView or a detach key invalidates it), and qa-worker's positive control now detaches a two-view buffer (decision 11); (2) real-GPU numbers: the freeze test's 1 s, boot time, FPS with the worker; (3) the G6 window (a crash between the worker's Ready and the scene) is covered by code only; (4) T039 (W1.3): the worker's journal, its IndexedDB and boot replay; (5) FallbackWorldView / FallbackObjectsView still miss a resync (decision 9).
T034b (the protector control; chain worker2): cloud/t034b, Nov 3-4; report docs/dev/reports/local-W1.2-worker.md, section "T034b, the protector control". qa-worker's positive control detaches a buffer with two TypedArray views (the no-view detach is a second negative control), so the worker's protector is gated in Chromium 153: intact after boot, the freeze, 10 minutes at speed 3 and in the founded city. qa-worker on the production build at size 256: 39 of 39 with --soak-min 10 --simwasm wasm, 35 of 35 without the soak and with ?simwasm unset. WorkerSimHost reads the packet's speed inside a packet's speedChanged (tests/worker/workerSpeed.test.ts; LoopbackSimHost stays T061's). tsc clean, full vitest 2,228 passed, bot identical to dev (residents [ 61124, 93804, 37971 ]).
